{
 "profile": "pq_key_binding.v1/cutoff-enforcement",
 "description": "Cutoff enforcement, v1. Admit an artifact iff PROVEN ANCHORED BEFORE the consumer cutoff, OR it carries a VALID PQ companion under the pq_pubkey of the binding IN FORCE at the artifact's anchor time (cutoff by ANCHOR TIME, consumer policy). v1 over v0: (1) an artifact anchored before the baseline's effective activation boundary B is admitted classical-only but NOT governed (resolved=null, pre_baseline) rather than retro-invalidated — the baseline governs only from B, no binding claims retroactive authority; (2) the verdict is tri-state — evidence in {verified, refuted, unverifiable}, decision a derived projection. A REVOCATION still ends authority at its anchor time: a post-revocation artifact is REFUTED even pre-cutoff, distinct from an innocent pre-baseline artifact. Each case asserts the resolution step, the evidence, the rule, AND the decision.",
 "v1_changes_from_v0": "(1) pre_baseline: an artifact anchored before the baseline's OWN anchor B is admitted classical-only but NOT governed (resolved=null, resolution_reason=pre_baseline, rule=pre_baseline_legacy_admit) — the baseline governs only from B, no binding claims retroactive authority; emitted fail-closed, only after the chain and B resolve. (2) tri-state evidence {verified, refuted, unverifiable}; decision is a derived projection. A revocation still ends authority at its anchor (post-revocation refused, distinct from pre_baseline). B is the EFFECTIVE ACTIVATION BOUNDARY: a binding's own anchor, or a later activated_at (delayed activation / pre-registration), clamped to >= binding_anchor_time. pre_baseline = anchored before B (including the dormant gap between a delayed binding's anchor and its activated_at); an activated_at < binding_anchor_time is malformed/unverifiable. An UN-ANCHORED binding (binding_anchor_time null) has no reproducible activation boundary and cannot govern: if no binding in the chain carries an immutable anchor the verdict is unverifiable/binding_anchor_unavailable/REJECT (derivability is not anchored authority); an un-anchored binding beside an anchored one is simply ignored.",
 "bindings": [
  {
   "name": "kya-l4-genesis",
   "secp256k1_pubkey": "0xFf9a176577Fb42b6bc9c19fd05a241e8fCd0ca14",
